        "side": "new",
        "severity": "high",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "MOV r/m64, imm32 now writes only 4 bytes to a memory destination",
        "explanation": "mov_rm_imm now passes std::mem::size_of::<$bound>() as the operand size to set_op. Because Mov_rm64_imm32 is instantiated with u32, that size is 4. MOV r/m64, imm32 (REX.W C7 /0) must sign-extend the imm32 and store 8 bytes. When the destination is memory, which is the usual case since this emulator handles MMIO exits, set_op writes only the low 4 bytes. The upper 4 bytes are left unchanged and the sign extension is lost, so the device sees a 4-byte write instead of an 8-byte one. The old u32tou64 variant wrote the full sign-extended 64-bit value. Register destinations still work, assuming get_op returns the sign-extended immediate32to64 value and write_reg writes the full register.",
        "suggestion": "Instantiate with the destination width: `mov_rm_imm!(u64);`. get_op still decodes the Immediate32to64 operand kind, so the 64-bit size is correct for both register and memory destinations. Also add a test for `mov qword [mem], imm32` with a negative immediate.",
        "evidence": "    mov_rm_imm!(u32);",
        "confidence": 0.75,
        "id": "f4f9b615b102",
        "hunk_id": "hypervisor/src/arch/x86/emulator/instructions/mov.rs#6",
        "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
