        "category": "bug",
        "title": "Mov_rm64_imm32 may now use a 4-byte operand size",
        "explanation": "The macro passes size_of::<$bound>() to get_op and set_op. With u32 that is 4. MOV r/m64, imm32 must sign-extend the immediate and write 8 bytes. The old u32tou64 type probably gave size 8. A memory destination could now get only 4 bytes written, and a register destination could lose its sign extension.",
        "suggestion": "Keep an operand size of 8 for this handler. Either pass the size separately from the type, or keep a type whose size_of is 8. Check that the immediate is sign-extended.",
